WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:07.320
Speaker 1: We have to absolutely huge stories
to start with today, and I wasn't sure which

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:10.210
to start with, but let's just start with the
first one.

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:16.759
We have now learned that Apple has given the
Trump or gave at the time the Trump administration

00:00:16.759 --> 00:00:21.510
information and documents on Democratic lawmakers.

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:29.789
And this is yet another attempted or real
abuse of subpoena power to obtain documents

00:00:29.789 --> 00:00:33.500
about the political enemies of the Trump administration.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:39.680
And we also, of course, have to consider the
role which Apple itself has played.

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:46.800
Let's take a look at an article from Thomson
Reuters which says Apple on Friday said it

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:52.970
has tightened some of its rules for responding
to legal requests after the U.S. Justice Department

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:58.989
during Donald Trump's presidency subpoenaed
it for information on Democratic lawmakers.

00:00:58.989 --> 00:01:03.630
Apple said it recently instituted a limit
of twenty five identifiers, such as email

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:06.840
addresses or phone numbers per legal request.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:11.380
So so far, what they're saying is, if you're
going to do this, you'll have to make multiple

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:12.380
requests.

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:14.479
You can't give us a list of one hundred identifiers.

00:01:14.479 --> 00:01:17.460
You'll have to give us four for lists of twenty
five.

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:21.560
The Cupertino, California based company said
it received a subpoena from the Justice Department

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:22.560
in February.

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:28.260
Twenty eighteen for information on one hundred
and nine identifiers made up of 73 phone numbers

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:33.289
and 36 email addresses, but that it did not
release content such as emails and pictures

00:01:33.289 --> 00:01:36.889
to prosecutors, The New York Times on Thursday
reported.

00:01:36.889 --> 00:01:41.149
And we will get to that report that federal
prosecutors subpoenaed Apple and other companies

00:01:41.149 --> 00:01:46.069
as part of an investigation, searching for
the sources behind media news reports about

00:01:46.069 --> 00:01:49.310
contacts between Trump's associates and Russia.

00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:50.679
This is a key line.

00:01:50.679 --> 00:01:52.619
What was the point of this?

00:01:52.619 --> 00:01:57.389
What was it that the Trump administration
at the Trump Justice Department was seeking

00:01:57.389 --> 00:02:00.920
to find out in requesting this information?

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:08.460
They were trying to uncover the sources, the
journalistic sources for reporting about Trump

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:10.690
administration contacts with Russia.

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:13.520
Think back to when this was going on.

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:17.830
And there were reports about Jeff Sessions
said there were no contacts.

00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:20.630
But look at all these contacts that we found.

00:02:20.630 --> 00:02:25.060
Donald Trump said there were no contacts,
the whole list of these people.

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:29.681
So the Trump administration through the Justice
Department said, hey, you know what, let's

00:02:29.681 --> 00:02:36.450
start figuring out let's get information from
people's iPhones and from the iCloud, from

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:39.030
the iCloud, whatever else was being used right.

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:41.760
Related to Apple or possibly being used.

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:49.660
Let's see if we can figure out who the sources
are or were for what these reports are claiming.

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:54.450
Trump publicly saying, oh, anonymous sources,
no, no, no, they're just bogus.

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:59.810
But privately, they knew they weren't bogus,
so much so that they were trying to figure

00:02:59.810 --> 00:03:02.690
out exactly who they were publicly saying.

00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:08.860
When you read anonymous source doesn't exist,
there's no one there's no real source privately

00:03:08.860 --> 00:03:14.500
understanding there are sources and trying
to figure out exactly who those people are.

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:18.510
The investigation targeted, at least to Democrats
on the House of Representatives Intelligence

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:25.030
Committee aides and family members, including
one minor, The New York Times reported.

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:28.960
Apple said it had no way to tell what the
nature of the investigation was and released

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:33.000
only basic account subscriber information
such as names, addresses, email addresses,

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:36.640
phone numbers as well as connection logs and
IP addresses.

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:44.430
Apple said it did not provide data showing
to whom or when messages of any kind were

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:45.430
sent.

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:52.090
The New York Times then reporting the Justice
Department subpoenaed Apple for information

00:03:52.090 --> 00:03:57.250
in February twenty eighteen about an account
that belonged to Donald F. McGann, the second

00:03:57.250 --> 00:04:00.640
president, Donald Trump's White House counsel
at the time.

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:02.570
This is another wrinkle to this story.

00:04:02.570 --> 00:04:07.240
This is another aspect which will we're still
trying to figure out for the most part, it

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:12.300
seems what was going on here was an attempt
to figure out who were the sources for the

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:19.950
news media, presumably on the Democratic side,
about these different contacts that the Trump

00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:22.000
campaign and administration had with Russians.

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:28.550
But at the same time, the New York Times report
points out that there was an attempt to get

00:04:28.550 --> 00:04:31.850
information about Donald Trump's lawyer as
well.

00:04:31.850 --> 00:04:37.350
And The New York Times article says it was
not clear what FBI agents were investigating,

00:04:37.350 --> 00:04:43.280
whether Mr. Morgan was there specific focus
or whether he was swept up in a larger net

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:45.840
because he had communicated with someone who
was under scrutiny.

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:48.590
That's another important aspect to understand.

00:04:48.590 --> 00:04:55.460
There are some on the right saying this was
not a partizan thing being done by Trump loyalists

00:04:55.460 --> 00:04:58.470
in the Justice Department looking for information
only.

00:04:58.470 --> 00:05:03.340
On Democrats, as evidenced by the fact that
they were looking for information about Trump's

00:05:03.340 --> 00:05:09.400
own lawyer, what it may have been, and if
it is, it's absolutely crazy that there was

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:11.740
some other person being scrutinized.

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:16.120
Imagine that there was just as a hypothetical,
some Russian national that was sort of at

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:17.560
the center of this.

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:21.430
The Justice Department may have been saying,
we need information on anybody who's been

00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:23.220
in touch with this person.

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:28.470
And Apple may have seen a connection between
Meghann and that individual.

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:32.130
And so, incidentally, Meghann may have been
swept up on it.

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:35.310
We just don't know at this point in time is
the point.

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:42.450
Now, meanwhile, as reported by CNN's Manu
Raju, who tweeted over the weekend, quote,

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:49.630
Bar sessions and now Rosenstein say they were
unaware of the subpoenas sent under their

00:05:49.630 --> 00:05:54.170
tenure for Democratic lawmakers records.

00:05:54.170 --> 00:05:57.280
These are three people with a track record
of dishonesty, first of all.

00:05:57.280 --> 00:05:59.370
So I wouldn't trust them much.

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:04.490
But what seems to be going on here is that
they are trying to get their stories straight

00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:07.740
for one word answers if they're ever forced
to testify.

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:10.460
How nobody knew anything.

00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:15.919
All of these subpoenas were filed, but nobody
knew who who authorized them, who signed.

00:06:15.919 --> 00:06:17.170
We just don't know.

00:06:17.170 --> 00:06:23.720
The administration was granted years long
gag orders against these subpoenas, same as

00:06:23.720 --> 00:06:24.720
the others.

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:28.550
These were gag orders that were renewed multiple
times.

00:06:28.550 --> 00:06:34.050
What judge okayed the renewal of the gag order
on the fact that these subpoenas were signed

00:06:34.050 --> 00:06:38.150
off on and granted which judge or judges were
involved?

00:06:38.150 --> 00:06:43.490
Do we need to subpoena the subpoenas to figure
out who is behind some of this stuff?

00:06:43.490 --> 00:06:46.750
It is an incredible story.

00:06:46.750 --> 00:06:51.560
It did not make the headlines, I might have
guessed it would have made or that that I

00:06:51.560 --> 00:06:53.780
would have hoped it would make.

00:06:53.780 --> 00:06:57.200
But a major story, which we are going to continue
following

